      "v": 8,
      "zh": "亚比筛对大卫说：「现在　神将你的仇敌交在你手里，求你容我拿枪将他刺透在地，一刺就成，不用再刺。」",
      "en": "Abishai said to David, “Today God has delivered your enemy into your hands. Now let me drive the spear[NOTE:1] right through him into the ground with one swift jab![NOTE:2] A second jab won’t be necessary!”",
      "notes": [
        "Here “the spear” almost certainly refers to Saul’s own spear, which according to the previous verse was stuck into the ground beside him as he slept. This is reflected in a number of English versions: TEV, CEV “his own spear”; NLT “that spear”; NIV11 “the spear.” Cf. NIV84, NCV “my spear,” in which case Abishai refers to his own spear rather than Saul’s, but this is unlikely since (1) Abishai would probably not have carried a spear along since such a weapon would be unwieldy when sneaking into the enemy camp; and (2) this would not explain the mention of Saul’s own spear stuck in the ground beside him in the previous verse.",
        "Heb “let me strike him with the spear and into the ground one time.”"
      ],
